.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_async_callback
sets an asynchronous callback function.
All
.Vt SSL
objects generated based on this
.Vt SSL_CTX
will get this callback.
If an engine supports the callback mechanism, it will be automatically
called if
.Sy SSL_MODE_ASYNC
has been set and an asynchronous capable engine completes a cryptography
operation to notify the application to resume the paused work flow.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_async_callback_arg
sets the callback argument.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set_async_callback
allows an application to set a callback in an asynchronous
.Vt SSL
object, so that when an engine completes a cryptography operation, the
callback will be called to notify the application to resume the paused
work flow.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_set_async_callback_arg
sets an argument for the
.Vt SSL
object when the above callback is called.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_async_status
returns the engine status.
This function facilitates the communication from the engine to the
application.
During an SSL session, cryptographic operations are dispatched to an
engine.
The engine status is very useful for an application to know if the
operation has been successfully dispatched.
If the engine does not support this additional callback method,
.Sy ASYNC_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED
will be returned.
See
.Xr ASYNC_WAIT_CTX_set_status 3
for a description of all of the status values.
.Pp
An example of the above functions would be the following:
.Bl -enum
.It
Application sets the async callback and callback data on an SSL
connection by calling
.Fn SSL_set_async_callback .
.It
Application sets
.Sy SSL_MODE_ASYNC
and makes an asynchronous SSL call
.It
OpenSSL submits the asynchronous request to the engine.
If a retry occurs at this point then the status within the
.Sy ASYNC_WAIT_CTX
would be set and the async callback function would be called (goto Step
7).
.It
The OpenSSL engine pauses the current job and returns, so that the
application can continue processing other connections.
.It
At a future point in time (probably via a polling mechanism or via an
interrupt) the engine will become aware that the asynchronous request
has finished processing.
.It
The engine will call the application's callback passing the callback
data as a parameter.
.It
The callback function should then run.
Note: it is a requirement that the callback function is small and
nonblocking as it will be run in the context of a polling mechanism or
an interrupt.
.It
It is the application's responsibility via the callback function to
schedule recalling the OpenSSL asynchronous function and to continue
processing.
.It
The callback function has the option to check the status returned via
.Fn SSL_get_async_status
to determine whether a retry happened instead of the request being
submitted, allowing different processing if required.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_async_callback ,
.Fn SSL_set_async_callback ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_async_callback_arg ,
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_async_callback_arg
and
.Fn SSL_get_async_status
return 1 on success or 0 on error.
